  "energy": "Hours of seated play with low energy demand; fitness supports health, posture and focus rather than in-game energy.",
  "summary": "Esports means long seated sessions with heavy hand and wrist use, and neck, back and wrist pain are common. The gym will not make you better at the game directly, but full-body strength, posture work and activity breaks protect your health and support focus.",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "claim": "In collegiate esports players, eye fatigue (56%), neck and back pain (42%) and wrist pain (36%) were common, and 40% did no physical activity.",
      "source": "DiFrancisco-Donoghue et al. 2019, BMJ Open Sport and Exercise Medicine",
      "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30792883/"
    },
    {
      "claim": "A 6 min walk during 2 h of play improved executive function compared with a seated rest, without affecting in-game performance.",
      "source": "DiFrancisco-Donoghue et al. 2021, BMJ Open Sport and Exercise Medicine",
      "url": "https://bmjopensem.bmj.com/content/7/3/e001118"
    }
  ],
